What: /sys/class/power_supply/axp20x-battery/charge_monitor
Date: November 2026
Description:
        Read-only AXP2101 Q2 charger observations, a versioned space-separated
        key=value line. Returns the register I/O errno on incomplete reads.
        version=1 reports thermal_regulation (live PMU_STATUS1 bit1),
        ts_monitoring (TS pin affects the charger), ts_adc_enabled,
        die_adc_enabled, battery_detection, ts_raw (-1 if ADC disabled),
        ts_valid (not disabled, saturated or overflowed), irq48_raw,
        irq4a_raw, and fault_history. The two IRQ bytes are historical W1C
        flags, never live fault assertions; reads do not clear them.
        fault_history ORs observed REG48[3:0] into bits3:0, REG4A[2:0] into
        bits10:8 since this driver probe. REG4A bit5 is reserved in V1.4,
        never diagnosed as battery overcurrent. There is no reset attribute.
        safe_mode_known=0 and battery_temperature_known=0 are explicit limits:
        no verified Battery Safe Mode state bit or pack thermistor calibration.
        A zero history is no observed fault, not a safety certification.
        Related standard health reports Safety timer expire for observed timer
        events, Over voltage for OVP, Unspecified failure for other observed
        faults or live die thermal regulation, otherwise Good. It is sticky
        history when an event has been observed, not a current battery-temperature
        claim. Charge behaviour auto is refused with EPERM for observed faults
        or thermal regulation, and fails on unreadable telemetry. Inhibition is
        always available independently of fault telemetry. No getter clears IRQs,
        resets the safety timer, or changes charger/protection policy.

What: /sys/class/power_supply/axp20x-battery/die_temperature_millicelsius
Date: November 2026
Description:
        Read-only PMIC die temperature in milli-degrees Celsius, not battery
        temperature. X-Powers AXP2101 FAQ V1.0 section2.8: T=22+(7274-ADC)/20.
        Reads the high byte before the low byte. ENODATA if ADC disabled,
        raw zero or conversion outside -40..150 degrees; I/O errors propagate.
        Probe enables only die ADC REG30 bit4 and restores its prior off state
        on removal/probe failure. Already-enabled channels remain enabled.
        This does not alter TS current source/monitoring, thermal thresholds,
        battery detection or other ADC channels, and is not a calibrated probe.

What: /sys/class/power_supply/axp20x-battery/ts_voltage_microvolts
Date: November 2026
Description:
        Read-only TS pin ADC voltage at 500 microvolts/code, not battery Celsius.
        ENODATA if ADC disabled, raw >=0x2000 (saturated/overflow; FAQ section2.12).
        I/O errors propagate. TS current source, thermistor wiring/calibration
        and charger coupling are separate; no temperature or pack presence can
        be inferred from a plausible TS voltage. No TS control write is made.

What: /sys/class/power_supply/axp20x-battery/charge_policy_control
Date: November 2026
Contact: Q2 Navidrome developers
Description:
 Read: version=1 epoch=<u64> generation=<u64> valid=<0|1>.
 Epoch is fresh at each driver probe. valid=0 forbids conditional control.
 Conditional authority is not published until all probe configuration succeeds.
 Write: <epoch> <generation> <inhibit|auto|current> <value>.
 inhibit/auto require value0; current uses an exactly representable microamp
 limit within the existing DT maximum. AUTO retains the observed-fault guard.

 Comparison and mutation share one driver mutex. Success consumes exactly one
 generation; the writer owns the predictable input generation+1, never a token
 obtained by a later read. An accepted hardware attempt which fails also
 consumes the generation, so no failed operation grants a replayable token.
 Reaching the final generation immediately publishes valid=0 (exhausted).
 Stale epoch/generation returns ESTALE without a hardware mutation. Counter
 exhaustion/unknown epoch return EOVERFLOW and keep conditional control closed.

 Standard charge_behaviour and constant_charge_current remain available.
 Every such legacy control attempt revokes previous policy authority, including
 same-value inhibition and failed hardware writes. Existing limits/protections
 remain unchanged and no IRQ status is cleared by the control interface.
 The public token is an ownership/version check, not a credential or safety
 certification. Reprobe/reset initialization rejects previously issued tokens.
